# Facts of the ask() keyword router (router.py:35-57). Each fact is one regex evaluated over the question; the host evaluates all of them (cheap), the rule order is the priority. ask.countActive is deliberately absent — its match is a no-op on the decided route (CANONICAL_PLANS["COUNT_ACTIVE"] is None; see ask/plans.py:27), confirmed by test_ask.py:test_router_count_active_falls_through_to_scene_query.
CONTRACT unitymcp.askroute
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE askroute_facts
FACT ask.mutating bool
FACT ask.unityNoun bool
FACT ask.brokenRefs bool
FACT ask.sceneHealth bool
FACT ask.editorState bool
FACT ask.compile bool
INPUT askRoute ask.mutating ask.unityNoun ask.brokenRefs ask.sceneHealth ask.editorState ask.compile
